# NumTalk 3D Platformer — Project Context

Self-contained mobile touch 3D platformer prototype (Mario lineage, not a clone). ~8-hour timebox. Built-in primitives only. Unity 6.x (6.3 LTS preferred) + New Input System + URP.

**Source of truth:** NumTalk Unity Developer Assignment PDF.

## Core loop (given, in order)

1. **RUN · PUSH** — camera-relative move with real accel/decel; walking into something moves it
2. **JUMP** — variable height; coyote + buffer on the player's side
3. **LAND / STOMP** — platforms answer back (move, ice, crumble); stomp enemy from above
4. **ADVANCE** — camera makes the next gap legible before commit
- **SHOT** — projectile knockback; does **not** cost a life
- **MISS OR HIT** — fall or side enemy hit → lose 1 of 3 lives → respawn at checkpoint
- **CHAIN** — reach the flag

## Build order (do not reorder; do not cut collision block)

1. **Movement** — camera-relative run, variable jump, coyote + buffer (named tunables)
2. **Touch input** — floating left stick, right tap jump, both thumbs simultaneous
3. **Camera** — third-person follow, damping, lead, no fight mid-jump, player stays on-screen at commit
4. **Platforms** — composable Moving / Ice / Crumble on **one** platform type (not three forked prefabs)
5. **Collision block** — pushable crate, shooter knockback, collision hygiene (layer matrix)
6. **Fail/checkpoint** — 3 lives, respawn, world state restore, game over at 0 lives (including third restart)
7. **Course** — one scene, 60–120s played well, goal flag; gaps within published max jump height/distance
8. **Should** — tuning ScriptableObject, one sudden event, feel juice
9. **Bonus** — only if above is solid

**Cut order if time runs out:** bonus → feel → sudden event → course length. **Do not cut the collision block.**

## Must build

- **Run** — floating virtual stick (left region); camera-relative accel/decel; both thumbs at once
- **Jump** — right-region tap; variable height (release early = hop); coyote + buffer as named tunables; document settled numbers
- **Camera** — third-person follow, damping, lead; no fight mid-jump; player not off-screen or behind geometry at commit
- **Land and stomp** — stomp from above: enemy dies, player bounces (holding jump = higher bounce); side/below = hit; must hold at full fall speed and 30 fps
- **Platforms** — Moving (ride + sensible jump-off velocity), Ice (low friction, momentum carries), Crumble (falls shortly after stood on); composable on one platform type
- **Fail and checkpoint** — fall or hit costs 1 life; respawn at last checkpoint with coherent world restore (document what you restore and what you don't); 0 lives = clean run end/restart
- **Course** — one authored course ending at goal; publish max jump height and max jump distance; every gap clears with margin
- **Frame-rate independence** — same feel at 30/60/120 fps; terminal-velocity fall must not tunnel through platforms; document how
- **Phone build** — Android APK, TestFlight, or device screen recording (two thumbs, not keyboard)

## Must: Collision (submission opens here first)

- **Push** — at least one landing blocked by a crate; real physical object (mass, friction); shove off edge, onto ice, stand and jump from it; never inside walls/floor; never push player through geometry
- **Get shot** — enemy fires projectile; hit does not cost a life; knockback impulse absorbed and decayed without losing control; composes with airborne, ice, moving platform, crate; knocked off ledge can kill
- **Collision hygiene** — projectiles: no tunneling, no friendly fire on shooter, no projectile-on-projectile; use **layer collision matrix** + collision detection mode, **not** tag checks in `OnTriggerEnter`; **layer layout in README**

## Should (if core is solid)

- One telegraphed sudden event mid-run (freeze, crumble-ahead, waking shooter, etc.)
- One tuning ScriptableObject (move, accel, jump, gravity, coyote, buffer, ice, crumble, crate mass, knockback + decay)
- Feel juice (squash/stretch, landing read, coin pop, stomp bounce, readable knockback)

## Bonus (only if above is genuinely done)

- Camera occlusion (pull in or fade blocking geometry)
- One original move (wall jump, ground pound, dash, double jump)
- Deterministic replay + "replay last run"
- Zero per-frame GC in movement loop; pooled projectiles/enemies/pickups + Profiler screenshot

## Hard constraints

- No third-party / asset-store platformer controllers or movement kits
- No Nintendo assets, characters, names, music, or level layouts
- Input System preferred over legacy Input
- One playable scene; readable git history (not a single initial commit)
- Frame-rate independent; no tunneling at 30/60/120 fps

## Out of scope

Menus beyond start + game-over overlay · art/models/textures/shaders · audio · saves/leaderboards/analytics/ads · localisation · settings screen · more than one course · test coverage beyond what helped you build · polished UI (coin counter + three life pips with default components is enough)

## Deliverables

- **Repository** — link or zip
- **Build** — APK, TestFlight, or device recording under 90 seconds
- **README** (one page) — Unity version, how to run, in/out, known issues, tuned movement numbers, **layer layout**
- **DECISIONS.md** (one page) — three hardest calls + trade-offs each; where you'd take the controller next; AI note (share of generated vs rewritten code, one thing assistant got wrong + how caught, one rejected suggestion + why)
